careful this video contains manga  spoilers the moment the eight-year-old  momos sacrificed his childhood to  transform into a full-grown dragon and  face his greatest fears head-on in order  to save his country i knew that we had  just witnessed the climax of one of the  best character arcs in one piece  what's an incredible turn around for the  traumatized and mistrusting little kid  that luffy found in the depth of punk  hazard where he then turned into a  full-fledged leader in a matter of  months being able to hear the voices of  all things he does not only possess one  of the rarest powers in the story but  his ability to command the titanic  elephant zonesha suggests that he holds  even greater power still all on top of a  ridiculously powerful devil fruit  and i'll even go so far as to claim that  the annoyingly perverted side of momo  that made me dislike the boy right from  the start was written on purpose by oda  to give us the most satisfying  development that we can get as a reader  from hate to love because over the  course of wano momo has gained more and  more of my respect and i can now say  that i absolutely love him as a  character which is good because i've  long been subscribed to the idea that  momo is set up to be one of the most  important characters in the story you  know just like you should be to this  channel okay so let's start by  addressing the biggest criticism people  have for momo usually his pervertedness  which is great because it's  coincidentally the secret ingredient to  the success of his character  [Music]  and you might be thinking now that i'm  giving oda too much credit here and  maybe i am but hear me out momo's  perverted nature differs from that of  sanji or brook which for some people  muddies these otherwise fantastic  characters in that a this is a little  kid and b he actually does the things  that brook and sanji would love to do  but can't and i think that's important  because for sanji and brook oda clearly  thinks that it's a funny character quirk  and the fact that sanji's peep attempts  always end in violence is probably  supposed to make it a likeable thing i  believe even if for most people it  probably isn't  [Music]  with momo on the other hand the smugness  with which he uses his young age to do  what he does even from oda's perspective  is clearly meant to piss you off even if  you're someone that has no problem with  sanji and brook and find their perkiness  hilarious momo would still annoy you for  his smugness and so in my eyes this is  clearly a trait that is meant to give us  a false bad first impression of momo  when we meet him i actually think that  momo got this quirk mostly from the  people he grew up with like kinemon odin  rayleigh who are all pretty infamous for  their love of women  later on in wano when yamato sticks him  inside her shirt to protect him he  actually doesn't think anything pervy at  all fully in the process of accepting  his uselessness and preparing to grow as  a character the truth here is is that  oda wanted you and me to dislike momo  from the start seeing him as a perverted  spoiled and useless kid holding everyone  back because this way his change as a  character would just be so much more  drastic that way now i don't want to  exonerate him completely here i'm sure  he genuinely loves those boobs but i  also think it's important to consider  that this is an eight-year-old who just  lost both his parents as well as his  sister mere days ago and is terribly  traumatized when we first meet him only  we don't know that yet of course and so  when he gets to bathe with and sleep in  the same room as nami and robin i think  this is actually momo looking for some  much needed motherly love rather than  anything else what makes momo's ark so  special in retrospect not only in one  piece but in storytelling overall is  that his development breaks with two  very established tropes the typical hero  shonen arcs are a that from a boy to a  man or b that from a man to a leader boy  to man actually has nothing to do with  age per se but simply means that a  character needs to leave the nest  question their naive ideas and learn to  face the real world basically a  coming-of-age story usopp for instance  falls really nicely into that pattern  now the arc from man to leader on the  other hand means that a character goes  from being concerned only for finding a  path for himself to realizing that he  must help others finding their way as  well zorro and sanji are great examples  of this  and since i guess you're curious luffy's  arc is that from leader to visionary  going from helping a few others find the  right path to changing the whole society  i've always loved how these storytelling  best practices explain why one piece  works so wonderfully as a story luffy of  course has the most important arc but  all other straw hats have their own  protagonist storyline as well now you  might have already figured out what  makes momo an odd one out here his  character arc basically forces him to  combine a and b and go from boy directly  to becoming a leader momo despite being  a normal kid is suffocating under the  expectations of an entire oppressed  nation to become the same great leader  that his father used to be before being  executed days before meeting luffy  [Music]  talk about a tough spot to be in momo is  still too young to become a man and far  from being the natural leader that luffy  is and so this gives momo the ultimate  arc to work his ass off to go through  not just one but two character changes  at once and that way faster and way  younger than most other characters in  one piece and so once i had that  complete set of information available to  me in wano momo's arc became a lot more  apparent and interesting after losing  his parents and being sent into the  future on top of everything else he also  gets separated from the only three  people that accompanied him at this  point by the way making khandro's  betrayal later on that much more  impactful  he then has to survive alone on punk  hazard with no time to mourn his dead  parents and his terrible fates and so  understandably when he's taken in by the  straw hats he is initially very  distrusting only revealing his true  identity on zou after having slowly  warmed up to the crew's kindness as well  as their strength  [Music]  and although even at this point he's  already trying to live according to all  the expectations put on his shoulders up  until though he basically is still a  traumatized kid always put in bubble  wrap by his retainers and then on though  he has his first real moment of  character growth after revealing his  true identity he tries to assume the  role of leader but  fails  again is the one to teach him an  important lesson in true leadership here  and so at this point momo understands  what he needs to do in order to form the  big alliance to take down kaido and save  his country because being a leader means  that you are the servant to your people  and not the other way around i was  actually also incredibly impressed by  the way that he handled sunisha a bit  later even though suddenly having a  depressed ancient giant elephant talking  to you in your head understandably might  come as a bit of a shock for an  eight-year-old  bravo momo  now it is on wano and more specifically  on igashima however where momo's arc now  comes to full bloom for me first of all  it was clear to me and to you as well  probably that breaching his home and  facing the aftermath of all the horrors  he had to live through there was  overwhelming for momo now that it was  actually time for him to assume his  position as leader he quickly comes to  terms with the fact that he is not the  person everyone wants him to be the son  of the endlessly charismatic and  powerful odin  and so momo unsurprisingly sinks into  self-doubt and leaves most of the  decision making to luffy and the  scabbards he just feels helplessly  pushed around by the events now  unfolding throughout the country and so  interestingly enough i found it took a  real shock for momo to come out of this  stupor it's actually the three most  scary events in wano so far that bring  out the best in him first he's betrayed  and taken hostage by conjuro one of the  few people he had trusted the most for  all this time  and still instead of feeling defeated he  starts to fight himself for the very  first time next even worse he gets put  on a crucifix in front of the man that  had killed his father  [Music]  and given the option to save his own  life as a [ __ ] eight-year-old kid he  decides to die for his beliefs and  declares himself shogen anyway of course  securing him the immediate respect of  all his followers and finally after  learning the important role he has to  play from his father's diary he is faced  with the prospect of onigashima crashing  into the flower capital and so reaching  the climax of his arc he decides to  sacrifice 20 years of his life as well  as his remaining childhoods and orders  shinobu to age him to 28 years old and  what makes this decision even more  important to me is that at this point he  doesn't take the scabbards wanting to  protect him as an excuse anymore what  made this so emotional for me was that  momo knew fully well that this won't  change the fact that he's still 8 years  old at heart but it gave him the chance  to fight and make a difference finally  he can now fly up and deal with the  problem himself this boy has the courage  to face all his fears at once heights  kaido and a responsibility to lead and  he passes with flying colors i think  watching luffy for all this time has  taught him the most important lesson of  all you have to take responsibility for  what happens to you otherwise you'll  never be able to change anything and so  it's actually not that surprising i  think that he takes the form of the two  men under whose shadow he had to live up  until now kaido as a dragon and odin as  a human finally prepare to assume his  role and surpass both of them as leaders  given all of his powers and whatever is  written about him in his father's diary  momo is bound to be one of the decisive  characters once we reach the endgame his  inspiration after all is momotaro the  hero who got accompanied by a monkey  luffy a dog yamato and a pheasant  possibly aokiji  [Music]  all you need to understand is why luffy  was the only one who could have turned  this eight-year-old traumatized kid into  the next shogun of one and this video  will tell you exactly why

